            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0779" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/960: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-24T13:00:00-05:00">April 24, 1935—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Your despatch No. 712 last two paragraphs.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d566-f1"/>
                    From the time of the Department’s telegram No. 14 of February 19, 1935, until
                    now we have been unable to begin negotiations for a trade agreement with Spain
                    as Calderón had received no instructions from Madrid. He notified us yesterday,
                    however, of the receipt of his instructions and stated that he was now prepared
                    to go forward with the negotiations. Copies of the lists of desiderata which
                    have already been exchanged are being forwarded to you and a list of our
                    proposed concessions to Spain will be sent you when they have received the
                    President’s approval. You will also be informed from time to time of the
                    progress of the negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
